{"name":"Pencil Eraser","hex":"#dbb7bb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pencil","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A writing utensil with a graphite (commonly referred to as lead) shaft, usually blended with clay, clad in wood, and sharpened to a taper. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","An aggregate or collection of rays of light, especially when diverging from, or converging to, a point."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To write (something) using a pencil.","To mark with, or as if with, a pencil."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pencil"},{"term":"eraser","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One who erases.","An object used to erase or remove something written or drawn by a pen or a pencil."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eraser"}],"entries":[{"title":"Eraser","blocks":[{"text":"An eraser is an article of stationery that is used for removing marks from paper or skin. Erasers have a rubbery consistency and come in a variety of shapes, sizes, and colors. Some pencils have an eraser on one end. Less expensive erasers are made from synthetic rubber and synthetic soy-based gum, but more expensive or specialized erasers are made from vinyl, plastic, or gum-like materials."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Office-pink-erasers.jpg/330px-Office-pink-erasers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eraser","wikidata":"Q171888"},{"title":"Pencil","blocks":[{"text":"A pencil is a writing or drawing implement with a solid pigment core in a protective casing that reduces the risk of core breakage and keeps it from marking the user's hand."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Pencils_hb.jpg/330px-Pencils_hb.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pencil","wikidata":"Q14674"}],"images